WEBVTT

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.510
Chaos

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.640
SHOGI HALL

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.600
Why?!

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.350
Unbelievable!

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.480
B BLOCK

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.480
FINALS

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.480
A BLOCK

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.730
I clawed my way up to C-1,
the same as you,

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:53.110
driven by desperation and thoughts
of the day I would play against you.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.610
TREMBLE
TREMBLE

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.610
So why can't we play against each other?

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.110
ZA-BAM

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.620
Are you being shy, Kiriyama?!

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.120
Ugh, so noisy.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.000
Why does he blame me?

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.000
BRISK
WALKING

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:11.380
We had more matches together at the kids'
tournaments back in elementary school!

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.590
There was no point in becoming a professional!

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.920
Then, we'll just have to...

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.840
become the winners of the Newcomer
Tournament's A Block and B Block,

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.970
and go up against each other in the finals,
otherwise we won't have

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.390
a single match together this year!

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.940
BRISK
WALKING

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.940
STOMP
STOMP

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.850
Kiriyama, don't tell me you're thinking,

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:35.110
"After all, the Newcomer Tournament
is full of newbies, so this'll be easy."

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.490
It's called the "Newcomer Tournament,"
but don't underestimate it!

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.610
I am not underestimating it.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.370
"KATSURA" ROOM

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.970
He made his move.
Kumakura 9th-Dan, Pawn to 2-7.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.230
Um, Kishou Yanagihara, at this current point,

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.860
who would you like to support,
Meijin Souya or Kumakura 9th-Dan?

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:23.410
Well, I don't want to support either of them.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.240
Be serious, Kiriyama!

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.870
- Arrogance leads to self-destruction!
- Pardon me.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.170
- Hey, Kiriyama.
- Yo.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.550
Yes, you're arrogant!

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.340
If I had to sum it up in one word,
it would be "chaos."

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.350
I'd go so far as to say
you're both arrogant and pompous!

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.640
I don't even know which of them is superior.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.970
Where do you get that from?

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.180
But I need something!
A headline for the internet!

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:45.810
From everything!

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.350
The prodigy who turned professional
in middle school, destined to become Meijin!

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.310
Okay, how about, "The Meijin Battle's
final game is a close contest."

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.980
You've been relying on that reputation!

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.190
But Mr. Yanagihara...

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.480
Ugh, it's so noisy.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.900
Issa, Smith.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.070
Throw those two out.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.320
Yep. At once.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.450
Yes, sir. Right away!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.120
Me too?

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.130
COMPACT...

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.590
Sheesh. That's what I hate about youngsters.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.970
Don't use words to fight. Settle it with shogi.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:24.890
Geez.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.260
Whoa. Souya moved his Rook to 3-7.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.230
Well, it's nice to see some enthusiasm,
don't you think?

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.770
I wish they would share a little
with their mentor.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.530
You mean Mr. Shimada?

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.200
Recently he's been lacking ambition, right?

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.320
It's like he's lost or something.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.910
Like you know, what happened to him?

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.200
In the Kishou Tournament qualifiers,

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.460
he kept making moves
that were unusual for him.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:55.330
Maybe Mr. Souya sucked the soul
right out of him?

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:00.460
It looks like even his shadow
has become lighter, you know?

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:05.390
In fact, his shadow's not the only thing
that's been thinning out!

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.220
Whoa, calm down a little!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.780
Guys who'll never get close to a title match
are so happy-go-lucky.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.160
<i>Gotou.</i>

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.830
Instead of worrying
about another player's mental health,

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.750
you should worry about your own life,
and the possibility that it could end

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:37.250
without ever being in a title match.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:44.880
Gotou.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:48.260
That's a bit harsh.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.270
Oh, Kumakura moved his Silver to 3-6.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.770
As expected. I thought he might do that.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.320
This is also...

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.190
...a good move.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:05.700
Dammit!

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.160
Let it go. Come on.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.950
There, you see? They left.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.670
Who cares. Probably went to the can.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.340
What are you going to do about this mood?

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:24.210
It's colder than ice in here now. Geez...

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.430
Everyone who's gotten their butts kicked
in a title match

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.850
will always lose their composure for a bit.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.600
That's just...

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.600
...how it is.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.110
"At this rate, I'll just lose."

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:47.110
That's what they come to realize
in between matches of a series.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:53.280
They have to break themselves apart, and then
reconstruct it again from the shattered pieces.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.410
They start over from square one.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.750
It's the same for everyone.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:09.800
Well, by "everyone," I mean players
who've experienced that.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.760
I'm sure if you leave Shimada alone,
he'll just start winning again.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.770
It just disgusts me...

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:25.780
to see people heckling others when they
themselves haven't even climbed into the ring.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:32.780
And so, you're always slashing up everything
like a knife itself.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.540
You're always so touchy.
What are you, a middle school student?

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.790
Geez, act like an adult already.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:44.040
GLOOMY

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.580
Excuse us.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.000
We haven't been in a title match at all.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.630
So how much time is left?
Is this Souya's side?

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.890
Sheesh. You don't listen, do you?

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.510
Kuma just passed the one hour mark.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.860
<i>Tell me, Rei. What should I do?</i>

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.280
<i>I'm...</i>

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.410
<i>...scared.</i>

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.460
<i>Stay away from my sister for now on!</i>

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:36.680
<i>You're married, aren't you?
What are you thinking?</i>

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.440
<i>People who can't cherish their family are trash!</i>

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.440
<i>Trash, huh? And also unforgivable?</i>

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.700
<i>What are you?</i>

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:54.030
<i>Who?</i>

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:55.910
<i>A god?</i>

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.370
<i>This is good. This is bad.</i>

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.580
<i>Are you the one who decides all that?</i>

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:08.960
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:12.840
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.680
<i>To me, humans are the embodiment of chaos.</i>

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.820
<i>The person
who got mad on Mr. Shimada's behalf</i>

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:32.190
<i>and the person
who makes my older sister suffer</i>

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.240
<i>are living in the same body.</i>

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.740
<i>How should I...</i>

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.540
Oh, he made a move.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.830
Souya moved his Pawn to 3-9,
and promoted it.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:47.130
What? Does he have time for that?

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.670
In that case, Bishop to 8-3.
And then, after that...

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:54.720
<i>Should I hate him?</i>

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.100
<i>Or...</i>

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.950
What is it, Gotou? You're leaving?

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.200
I have a match tomorrow.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.620
Don't make Kouda cry too much.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.310
Why do you always have this fierce stance?

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:49.730
Fierce? Are you saying I look like an ogre?

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:51.820
Then you're already aware of it.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.690
ANGER ANGER ANGER ANGER

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.010
What's wrong, Kiriyama?

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:17.090
Oh, uh...

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.090
It's nothing.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:26.060
<i>For some reason,
I suddenly had the feeling she was near.</i>

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.650
<i>The last time I saw her was in March.</i>

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.400
<i>I thought about calling her after that,</i>

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.570
<i>but I stopped when I reached for the phone.</i>

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.990
<i>What should we even talk about?</i>

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.170
<i>Even if she were close to me,
the one standing next to her is...</i>

00:11:53.840 --> 00:12:00.090
Sometimes it'll look simple to unravel,
but other times it looks messed up and tangled.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.470
If I had to put it in one word...

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:11.480
<i>Then Mr. Yanagihara paused
for a moment before muttering...</i>

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.900
"Chaos."

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:19.990
Chaos

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:23.990
Kumakura

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:31.500
The seventh game on the second day
of the 69th Meijin Battle.

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:36.290
It's been a close contest that has required
a full set of games, but this is the final game.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:38.840
This game will decide the winner.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.390
<i>Because of the dinner break,</i>

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:52.100
both players have less time,
but their expressions look calm.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:59.820
Meijin Souya has won five times, totaling 11 wins.
Will he retain the title of "Meijin" today?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:08.030
Or will Kumakura 9th-Dan, the challenger
for the fourth time in a row, seize the title?

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:16.880
Ah, Meijin Souya has made his move.
Bishop to 4-4.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.380
This is...

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.970
<i>What do you think, commentator Mr. Tsujii?</i>

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:26.890
Tsujii 9th-Dan at The Match's Commentary Hall

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.890
<i>This is an unusual move.</i>

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.940
Why did he do that?

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:38.060
It's not a Bishop to 3-7 promotion,
nor is it a Dragon to 3-7.

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.740
It feels like he wasted a move.

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:56.000
It doesn't have any special meaning.

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:03.260
That's because this is a free-for-all.
It's like saying, "Go ahead, think about this."

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:05.510
It happens.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:09.850
I don't think even Souya
would know what to do anymore.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.350
I get it. Yes, yes.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:19.110
<i>Then at this stage, could we say
Kumakura 9th Dan has a slight advantage?</i>

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:20.610
BAM

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:24.650
Indeed! I'm sure Kumakura 9th Dan
will do a dodge move next.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:26.400
He'll probably make his move quickly.

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:38.380
Wait. This is...

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:44.050
I lost.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:49.220
What? Oh, he resigned.
Kumakura 9th Dan has resigned!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.850
Meijin Souya has defended his title!

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.560
R-Resigned?!

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.100
Wait a second! Suddenly?

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.680
Hey, get the camera!

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:58.020
- The observer isn't even in there!
- Hello? He resigned!

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.060
- Hurry!
- Where's Mr. Nakamura, the observer?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:03.190
Kumakura resigned. I said, he resigned!
Please hurry!

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:09.160
Huh? Resigned? All of a sudden?

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:11.660
Mr. Kumakura, why?

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:14.910
Wasn't that too soon? He still had moves...

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.580
I mean, I thought he had the upper hand.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:24.840
No. He was checkmated.
At precisely the 17th move.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.100
King, same.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:46.820
Pawn to 1-4.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.120
Lance, same.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:55.700
King, same.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.690
It's true.

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:26.440
<i>No one noticed.</i>

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.820
<i>But when it's played out, there's no denying it.</i>

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:35.080
<i>At this point, he was trapped,
no matter where he moved.</i>

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.620
<i>It's all in vain.</i>

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.830
Souya.

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.000
Brilliant.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.220
I didn't train enough.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.090
That's all I can say.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:57.430
For this next year, I'll fight off everyone
in the rank-deciding competitions

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:00.850
and train hard
so I can come back and sit here again.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.690
Oh, man. He's so cool.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:06.230
K-Kumakura 9th Dan gives me goosebumps!

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:08.110
I want to be like him!

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:11.360
How can he be so calm about it?

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:13.820
Right after a full set of matches?

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.370
Ah, Kengo is so cool!

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.120
<i>Is it confidence?</i>

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:30.550
<i>Starting at square one and fighting through
Class A, the den of demons, over and over,</i>

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:36.140
<i>swearing that he'll be sitting
in front of the champion next year, too...</i>

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.480
Sorry I took so long.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:53.740
Here, toner, lotion, and they had a new
moisturizing cream, so I tossed that in.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:54.990
I think that should do it.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:01.620
Sorry for the hassle. I won't stop sneezing
if I go into places like that.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:05.500
VACANT

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.120
TAKEN

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:08.380
See you. Thanks again.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.720
Want me to go with you?

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.300
I'll thank you properly next time.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:20.970
Later.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.220
Central Hospital.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:05.350
Hey.

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:07.270
I'm here.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:09.810
Misako.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:42.180
You're late!

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:43.600
Why are you here?

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:46.520
Here. I picked these up for you.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.850
You were collecting too many claim checks.

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:51.440
Claim checks? From my wallet earlier!

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.690
Enough. Get up.

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.110
I'll throw you in a taxi.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.070
PHOOEY

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.950
Forget it. I'm staying over.

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:02.990
No way. If I did that,
you would definitely attack me.

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:04.240
A-Attack?

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:04.240
98% BULLSEYE

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.620
I-I wouldn't!

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.620
BLUSH

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:10.210
Then never mind. I'm leaving!
I'm going home!

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:11.580
Good.

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.630
Will you walk me to the taxi stand?

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.960
Yeah, sure.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.260
Why don't you at least
put your dry cleaning inside?

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:20.380
Oh, right.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.130
GLEAM

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:31.810
When all is said and done,
your defenses are weak, huh?

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.900
That's why I take advantage of you.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:37.530
Whatever, just go home.
I'm really tired.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.780
That's okay, just go to sleep.
Pay me no attention.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.950
Fine. You're so troublesome. Come here.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.200
PING

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:45.870
SHINE

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:51.920
What? Hey, what is this?

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:53.920
Goodnight.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:58.590
H-Hey! What is this? Untie me!
How could you!

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:03.340
My clothes will get wrinkly!
And I need to get my makeup off! Hey!

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:04.140
ROLL

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.220
GRAB

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.030
<i>Deep shadows under his eyes...</i>

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:26.530
<i>He probably hasn't slept well in a long time.</i>

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:28.870
<i>His face is pale.</i>

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:32.750
Ugh... Idiot.

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:35.500
<i>Now I can't get mad at you.</i>

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:39.170
<i>Not after you show me this face.</i>

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:45.050
<i>The next day,</i>

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:49.390
<i>Kumakura 9th Dan took the early morning
limited express train and left Hakone behind.</i>

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:55.900
Um, Chairman, excuse me...

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:58.230
Huh? What is it?

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:03.320
When we entered the room
to clean it this morning...

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:03.320
CRUMBLE

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:05.700
...it was in this state.

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:06.950
RUINED

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:08.490
I thought I should show it to you.

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:13.290
Kumakura! That bastard!

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:17.790
<i>It's not funny!</i>

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:22.380
I see! So he kicked the hell out of the wall.
That Kuma!

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:28.010
He is definitely going to pay
for the damages and a severe penalty!

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:33.680
I'll send him to shogi events on department store
rooftops during sweltering summer vacation!

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:38.190
To think he would
kick a hole in the wall after losing.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:41.780
Oh, Kuma.

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:47.950
I get it though. It must have been frustrating.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.080
It couldn't have been
anything other than frustrating.

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Kumakura

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:39.140
Episode 25

00:24:32.340 --> 00:24:34.970
First we both have to clear
the qualifying round.

00:24:34.970 --> 00:24:39.140
I didn't know that cool-looking person
has been hiding such passion.

00:24:39.140 --> 00:24:43.360
On the surface, it seemed cool,
like a good match for cold, green tea.

00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:46.940
Let's see... A duck?

00:24:46.940 --> 00:24:50.030
It all brings back memories.

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:53.620
"March Comes in Like a Lion".
Please watch it next time too.

00:24:53.620 --> 00:24:58.040
Kumakura! I need to talk to you!
